WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.580
A rat hears a tone that once came before a mild shock.

2
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.640
It freezes, and its blood pressure rises.

3
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.980
Does one pathway carry both responses?

4
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.880
Neither response is the feeling of fear, but both can be measured.

5
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:22.153
First, is the response learned?

6
00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:26.113
One group of rats hears tones that predict shocks.

7
00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:32.493
A control group hears the same tones and shocks, never together, so only the

8
00:00:32.493 --> 00:00:33.593
difference is learning.

9
00:00:34.673 --> 00:00:41.073
In invented numbers, paired rats froze for 60% of the tone, and unpaired rats for

10
00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:43.953
eight, a learned difference of 52 points.

11
00:00:45.193 --> 00:00:50.333
Pressure rose 20 millimetres of mercury in paired rats, and three in unpaired rats,

12
00:00:50.813 --> 00:00:52.233
a learned difference of 17.

13
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:58.227
In the rat, the tone reaches the lateral amygdala, the input stage.

14
00:00:59.207 --> 00:01:02.187
The central amygdala then sends outputs onward.

15
00:01:03.307 --> 00:01:06.027
One route runs through the lateral hypothalamus.

16
00:01:06.947 --> 00:01:12.287
Another runs through the caudal periaqueductal gray, the sheath of neurons around

17
00:01:12.287 --> 00:01:13.827
the midbrain's fluid canal.

18
00:01:15.047 --> 00:01:16.867
Which route carries which response?

19
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:25.067
Now cut one route, and ask how much of what was learned is left, after taking away

20
00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:26.747
the unpaired baseline.

21
00:01:28.127 --> 00:01:34.767
Lesion the lateral hypothalamus: freezing keeps 94%, but the pressure rise keeps

22
00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:40.987
only 6. Lesion the caudal periaqueductal gray, and it reverses.

23
00:01:41.547 --> 00:01:45.307
Freezing keeps 2%, and pressure keeps 94.

24
00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:52.840
Lesion the central amygdala, and both responses fall to about zero, as a shared

25
00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.580
source for the two routes predicts.

26
00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.120
Each output lesion removed one response and kept the other.

27
00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:05.480
That is a double dissociation: two separate routes below one amygdala node.

28
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.820
It locates the outputs of a defensive response.

29
00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.320
It says nothing yet about a feeling.

30
00:02:12.333 --> 00:02:19.333
Patient SM has damage to both amygdalae, and reported at most minimal fear to the

31
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:20.653
external threats tested.

32
00:02:21.513 --> 00:02:27.713
Yet she and two other women with that damage all panicked after one breath of 35%

33
00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:30.973
CO2. Three of twelve comparison women did.

34
00:02:31.733 --> 00:02:34.673
The difference lay in the threat, not the patient.

35
00:02:35.893 --> 00:02:40.433
Rat work can find necessary steps for a measured response, under defined conditions.

36
00:02:40.433 --> 00:02:45.993
It cannot say what the animal feels, or that a human feeling takes the same route.
